/// Lesson sections for the info page — never shown on the practice screen.
const List<TechniqueSection> setAroundTheKitLesson = [
  TechniqueSection(
    title: "Why it matters",
    body:
        "Toms and cymbals are where the kit stops being a pad. This sheet sends plain stickings round all four toms and gives each line a different cymbal on the one: crash in lines 1 to 3, china in lines 4 to 6, ride bell in lines 7 and 8. Your hands learn the distances, and the cymbal becomes a choice.",
  ),
  TechniqueSection(
    title: "How to play it",
    body:
        "Each line has two bars: a rock eighths groove with the line's cymbal on the one instead of the hi-hat, then the figure, one drum per beat, kick on 1 and 3 underneath. Line 1 plays sixteenths on snare, high tom, mid tom and floor tom; line 2 the same from the high tom down to the second floor tom. Move in a flat arc with the sticks low and arrive on each drum on the beat.",
  ),
  TechniqueSection(
    title: "Practice tips",
    body:
        "Line 3 alternates paradiddles between the snare and the toms. Line 4 plays sextuplets down the toms, line 5 accents 6-6-4 (1, the \"and\" of 2, and 4) while the drums change on the beats, line 6 is doubles on high tom, floor tom and second floor tom. Line 7 is one flam per drum, line 8 has a beat of thirty-seconds on the floor tom; both return to the ride bell, played with the shoulder of the stick. The china accepts any crash, the toms any tom, so fewer drums work too.",
  ),
  TechniqueSection(
    title: "Where you hear it",
    body:
        "Tom runs at the end of a drum solo, china accents in metal and fusion, and the ride bell on top of rock choruses and Latin grooves.",
  ),
];
